Sorry M8s.. No "real" Documentation Is Available Yet.. This Is
Only An 4-Hour-Production And I Don`t Want To Write A Big Doc
For This Tool.. It`s A Simple-To-Install XiM-Door.. You Can
Use The Following Tooltypes In LastAvail.info...


==[ Example Configration For LastAvail.Info ]===============[ WD/MtS^SCX ]==

DEFAULT_NUMBER=+49-PRI-VAT-E!
NUMBER.1=+49-471-718-54
NUMBER.2=+49-RING-DOWN!

NODESTATUS.0=HIDDEN
NODESTATUS.1=NONE
NODESTATUS.2=SILENT

FAKE_NODE_NUMBERS.0=NO
FAKE_NODE_NUMBERS.1=NO
FAKE_NODE_NUMBERS.2=NO

FRONTEND_START.0=FRONTEND
FRONTEND_CLEAR.0=NO
FRONTEND_WAIT.0=NO
FRONTEND_WHO.0=NO
SYSOP_NAME.0=NO

FRONTEND_START.1=WHO
FRONTEND_CLEAR.1=NO
FRONTEND_WAIT.1=NO
FRONTEND_WHO.1=YES
SYSOP_NAME.1=YES

MESSAGE_START.0=MESSAGE1
MESSAGE_CLEAR.0=YES
MESSAGE_WAIT.0=NO
MESSAGE.0=Der Sysop ist der einzig wahre Held!
MAXMESSAGES=1

============================================================================

DEFAULT_NUMBER={string}

LastAvail Will Use {string} As A Default-Phonenumber For Your Nodes

============================================================================

NUMBER.{x}={string}

LastAvail Will Use {string} As The Phonenumber For Node {x}

============================================================================

NODESTATUS.{x}={string}

{string}=SILENT - LastAvail Will Set The "Action" and "User"-Fields For
                  Node {x} To "-Silent Mode!-" if It Was Started On Another
                  Node Than {x}.

{string}=HIDDEN - LastAvail Will Not Display The Node-Informations For
                  Node {x} if It Was Started On Another Node Than {x}

============================================================================

FAKE_NODE_NUMBERS.{x}={yes/no}

LastAvail Will Use "Fake"-Nodenumbers For The Frontend-Mode {x} If You
Set {yes/no} to "YES".. f.ex.:

{yes/no}="NO" (Node 0 Is Set To "HIDDEN" Using The NODESTATUS-Tooltype)
--[ LastAvail v0.4 ]--- -- ---- ------- ----- ---- ---- -- --[ WD/MtS^SCX ]--

 [ Node ]-----[ User ]------v---------[ Action ]---------v----[ Number ]---.
 ¦  01  ¦ No User Online    ¦ Waiting For A Call         ¦ +49-471-718-54  ¦
 ¦  02  ¦ -Silent Mode!-    ¦ -Silent Mode!-             ¦ +49-RING-DOWN!  ¦
 `------^-------------------^----------------------------^-----------------'

             the sysop wicked dream is not around to chat with you

------ - ------ -- ----- ---- ---------- ----- ---- ------- --------- -------

{yes/no}="YES" (Node 0 Is Set To "HIDDEN" Using The NODESTATUS-Tooltype)
--[ LastAvail v0.4 ]--- -- ---- ------- ----- ---- ---- -- --[ WD/MtS^SCX ]--

 [ Node ]-----[ User ]------v---------[ Action ]---------v----[ Number ]---.
 ¦  00  ¦ No User Online    ¦ Waiting For A Call         ¦ +49-471-718-54  ¦
 ¦  01  ¦ -Silent Mode!-    ¦ -Silent Mode!-             ¦ +49-RING-DOWN!  ¦
 `------^-------------------^----------------------------^-----------------'

             the sysop wicked dream is not around to chat with you

------ - ------ -- ----- ---- ---------- ----- ---- ------- --------- -------

============================================================================

FRONTEND_START.{x}={command}

{x}			=	0-10
{command}	=	The Command LastAvail Was Started With (f.ex. ANSI, WHO, ..)

============================================================================

FRONTEND_CLEAR.{x}={yes/no}

{x}			=	0-10
{yes/no}	=	If You Set This Value To "YES", LastAvail Will Clear The
				Screen If It Was Started Using The FRONTEND_START.{x}
				Command. (Review The Example Configuration In The
				Distribution-Archive)

============================================================================

FRONTEND_WAIT.{x}={yes/no}

{x}			=	0-10
{yes/no}	=	If You Set This Value To "YES", LastAvail Will Wait For
				Any Key Entered By The Online User Before It Exits..

============================================================================

FRONTEND_WHO.{x}={yes/no}

{x}			=	0-10
{yes/no}	=	If You Set This Value To "YES", LastAvail Will Display
				The Online Users Too (Handle/Name), If It Is Set To
				"NO" It Will Display NodeNumba, Action And Phone-# Only.

============================================================================

SYSOP_NAME.{x}={yes/no}

{x}			=	0-10
{yes/no}	=	If You Set This Value To "YES", LastAvail Will Display
				The Sysop`s Name In The "The Sysop Is.. For Chat" Message.

f.ex.:
If {yes/no} is set to "NO", LastAvail Will Display The Following Message
After The Node-Information:

the sysop is (not) available for chat

If {yes/no} is set to "YES", LastAvail Will Display The Following Message
After The Node-Information:

the sysop {sysopname} is (not) available for chat

============================================================================

MESSAGE_START.{x}={command}

{x}		=	0-{value set in MAXMESSAGES-Tooltype}
{command}	=	The Command LastAvail Was Started With

If You Start LastAvail With {command}, It Will Display The Message
Given In Tooltype "MESSAGE.{x}"... It Will Wait For Any Entered Key
If You Set The "MESSAGE_WAIT.{x}" Tooltype To "YES" And Will Clear The
Screen If You Set The "MESSAGE_CLEAR.{x}" Tooltype To "YES"..

============================================================================

MAXMESSAGES={x}

{x}		=	Max. Numba Of Message-Commands You Want Install In LastAvail

============================================================================

If You Have Any Problems With The Installation Of My Tool - Simply Don`t
